 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
 *   **Limited Registers:** It is not possible to write initial values to the two spare registers displayed in Fig. 2 of the source, limiting the ability to add a second diffuse light source without sacrificing trilinear interpolation or separate ambient/diffuse colors [S2].
-*   **Signed Values:** The method relies on signed fixed-point values in the general combiner stages. If the hardware does not support this, vector components must be scaled and biased to the positive range, which is not required here [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Single-Pass Limitation:** While efficient, this method is limited to the number of available combiner stages and registers. Complex lighting models requiring more than one diffuse light source or specular highlights may not be feasible without compromising other features [S2].
+*   **Signed Values:** The method relies on signed fixed-point values in the general combiner stages [S1, unofficial]. If the hardware does not support this, vector components must be scaled and biased to the positive range, which is not required here [S1, unofficial].
